l","cover_id":14425151,"author_id":987300009,"work_type":"novel","source_type":"open_library","open_library_id":"OL20787872W","first_publish_year":2020,"native_identity_key":"nlscale:20261102:ol:OL20787872W"},"before_row":null},{"key":{"open_library_edition_id":"OL41872216M"},"seq":80,"relation":"editions","after_row":{"id":987203017,"title":"De wachtpost","isbn_10":null,"isbn_13":"9789024591947","work_id":987103017,"cover_id":14425151,"language":"dut","publisher":"Uitgeverij Luitingh-Sijthoff","publish_date":null,"open_library_edition_id":"OL41872216M"},"before_row":null},{"key":{"work_id":987103017,"language":"nl"},"seq":81,"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","after_row":{"text":"Jack Reacher stapt uit de bus in een stadje bij Nashville, met weinig meer plannen dan koffie drinken en verder reizen. Een digitale aanval heeft het plaatselijke leven echter ontregeld. IT-medewerker Rusty Rutherford lijkt meer met de problemen te maken te hebben dan hij zelf beseft en wordt door gevaarlijke mannen belaagd. Reacher grijpt in. Zijn korte tussenstop verandert in een onderzoek naar wie het stadje heeft getroffen en waarom Rusty daarbij een doelwit is geworden.","work_id":987103017,"evidence":[{"note":"Original publisher announcement22Jan2020 explicitly resolves Andrew Grant=Andrew Child, names The Sentinel and2020 publication. Exact Dutch De wachtpost9789024591947 and front match; no duplicate author or Work, no new special-edition content inferred.","type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p427620007","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p433000155"],"reference":"new-work-dossier-readings-004.json#140","checked_at":"2026-11-02T17:16:06.000Z"},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","review":"content-review-010.json","sources":["https://global.penguinrandomhouse.com/announcements/lee-childs-new-jack-reacher-co-author-his-brother-andrew-grant/","https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/635231/the-sentinel-special-edi